  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Pibada-style opera is the North Korean form launched with Sea of Blood (1971) and The Flower Girl (1972), the first two of the Five Great Revolutionary Operas. It replaces aria and recitative with strophic songs (jeolga), adds an offstage chorus (pangchang) that comments on the action, and sets them for a mixed orchestra of Western and Korean instruments; generic string and horn cards stand in for the orchestra.",
